        ":question/problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u={log}_{5}\u2061x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}\\,\u27f9\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20615\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{x{log}_{5}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{5}^{25}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20615\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u20615{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u20615(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u20615(\\operatorname{ln}\u20612-\\operatorname{ln}\u20611) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u20612\\operatorname{ln}\u20615\\end{aligned}\n$$",
